\section{The geometry is simplified}{

The upstream onshore boundaries are 13 MB of GeoJSON. They are reduced with
\code{rmapshaper::ms_simplify(keep = 0.03, keep_shapes = TRUE)}, which drops
vertices while guaranteeing every polygon survives — islands included; the
build script refuses to save an object that lost a region.

It is therefore a \strong{display} geometry. Do not compute areas or distances
from it. Rebuild at full resolution from a PyPSA-Eur clone with
\code{pypsa_geo_layers()} and \code{pypsa_geoscale()} if you need those.

No map ships for \link{pypsa_eur_5}; its GeoJSON sidecars are in the package
instead, reachable through \code{\link[=reneuro_example_geo]{reneuro_example_geo()}}.
}

